We have the matrix
\[ A = \begin{pmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end {pmatrix}. \]Then
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end {vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end {vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cot^2 x \end {vmatrix} + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x \end {vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \sec^2 x \csc^2 x \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \csc^2 x \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x (1 - \cos^2 x) + \cos^2 x (\cos^2 x - 1) \\ &= \cot^2 x \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x (1 - \sin^2 x) \\ &= \cos^2 x (\cos^2 x) = \cos^4 x. \end{align*}
The determinant can only be 0 or 1. Its range is $[0,1]$, depending on $x$.

However, we are asked to find all possible values. Let
$f(x) = \cos^4 x$.
When $x = 0$, $f(x) = \cos^4 0 = 1^4 = 1$.
When $x = \frac{\pi}{2}$, $f(x) = \cos^4 \frac{\pi}{2} = 0^4 = 0$.
\[ f'(x) = 4 \cos^3 x (-\sin x) = -4 \cos^3 x \sin x \]
The possible values are in $[0,1]$.

\boxed{ \cos^4 x }
