Here is a math problem written in LaTeX: The equation of the  hyperbola shown below can be written as
\[\frac{(y - k)^2}{a^2} - \frac{(x - h)^2}{b^2} = 1.\]Find $h + k + a + b.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.3 cm);

real upperhyper (real x) {
  return (2*sqrt((x - 6)^2/16 + 1) - 5);
}

real lowerhyper (real x) {
